ED 2026-10-09 on $VIMRUNTIME/lua: 832 edges landed on stubs; 67 real functions `pure` → `io`, 134 `pure~` → `io~`, 17 → hedged. CART-1615 |\n| Does a call's effect reach a caller whose ARGUMENTS rule its branch out — `vim.validate('s', s, 'string')` never takes the deprecated `elseif type(name) == 'table'` arm? | `effects.purity` / `summaries` already answer it. A Lua call record carries `gp` (±param, `M._call_gp`): it runs only while param i is truthy (+) or falsy (−). That holds in a then-arm whose condition is the param (or a conjunction over it), and in an else or ELSEIF arm of `if <param>`. Everything the call brings in (keys → `gpk`, hedges → `gh`) carries the site's guard, and `M.verdict` discharges it at each caller from the argument there (a literal, or a missing argument = nil). A key added unguarded, or under another guard, is unguarded. An undecided guard makes a write conditional (tier ≥ 2), never stronger. A guarded edge that closes a cycle is cut from the condensation (vim.validate ↔ vim.deprecate), so each member keeps its own summary; the cut site takes the previous pass's summary. Single-member components only. MEASURED 2026-10-09: $VIMRUNTIME/lua 168 writes~ → io~, 140 writes~ → pure~; lua/cartograph 5 writes~ → pure~ (240 discharged keys), summaries 3.0 → 2.4 s. CART-1567 |"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},"bytes":1195,"decided_by":"tactic"}],"hand":0}
